# Constitution

## Engineering Principles
- Extend, don't rewrite. All changes build on existing code.
- In-memory only. No databases, no WebSockets, no auth.
- TypeScript strict. No `any`. Prefer `unknown` for dynamic types.
- Server is single source of truth. Client is a view layer.
- Validate all inputs server-side with Zod.

## AI Usage Rules
- AI may draft code, but the author must read and understand every line before committing.
- AI must not generate out-of-scope features (multi-round, timers, WebSockets, etc.).
- AI must check existing conventions before writing new code.

## Review Discipline
- Test with two browser tabs after each feature group.
- Spec must be updated before implementation of that group begins.
- Commit granularly: one logical change per commit.
- Run `npm run build` in both backend and frontend before final commit.
